# macOS localization

Follow the project skill `.cursor/skills/add-localized-string/SKILL.md`. Full notes: `docs/macos-client-patterns.md` § Localization.

- User-facing copy: `L10n.*` only. No hard-coded English (or raw catalog keys) in views/models.
- Decorative punctuation, brand, **numbers/ordinals**, and other non-translated glyphs: `Text(verbatim:)` — never bare `Text("…")` or `Text("\(…)")`, or `SWIFT_EMIT_LOC_STRINGS` will re-inject junk keys (`%lld`, `%@`, `""`) into `Localizable.xcstrings` on every build.
- Unlabeled form controls: never `TextField("", …)` / `Picker("", …)` — use `TextField(text:prompt:) { EmptyView() }` or `Picker(selection:) { … } label: { EmptyView() }` (empty title extracts as catalog key `""`).
- Interpolated accessibility values: `Text(verbatim: "\(title), \(ref)")` — never `"\(x)"` / `Text("\(count)")` as `LocalizedStringKey`.
- After touching SwiftUI `Text`, run `python3 scripts/check-localizable-xcstrings.py` and discard accidental catalog churn.
- CI: `scripts/check-localizable-xcstrings.py` (macOS workflow) rejects non-dotted keys, `extracted_with_value`, and `isCommentAutoGenerated`.
- Add/change a string in **both** [`macos/App/Platform/L10n.swift`](macos/App/Platform/L10n.swift) and [`Localizable.xcstrings`](macos/App/Resources/Localizable.xcstrings) (or `InfoPlist.xcstrings` for Info.plist keys). Prune both when removing.
- Keys: semantic dotted (`onboarding.chooseFile.welcomeTitle`). Nest by feature under `L10n`.
- Interpolated copy: static key + `%@` in catalog/`defaultValue`, then `String(format:locale:_:)`.
- Stable `.accessibilityIdentifier` for UI tests — not localized titles.
- Do not localize by matching English Go strings. FFI failures are protobuf codes → `L10n.Errors`. No SwiftGen.

```swift
// ❌ BAD
Text("Welcome to Provenencia")
Text("\(index + 1)")           // extracts as %lld
Button(L10n.Onboarding.signOut) { … }  // needs StringProtocol on macOS 14 / CI Xcode 16

// ✅ GOOD
Text(L10n.Onboarding.welcomeTitle)
Text(verbatim: "\(index + 1)")
Button(String(localized: L10n.Onboarding.signOut)) { … }
```
